Package: dlna-gmediarender-kde
Version: [[VERSION]]
Section: sound
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: gmediarender, gstreamer1.0-plugins-base, gstreamer1.0-plugins-good, gstreamer1.0-plugins-bad, gstreamer1.0-plugins-ugly, gstreamer1.0-libav, pactl
Maintainer: Grégory D <rginon314@github.com>
Description: KDE Plasma 6 applet to receive DLNA audio and switch output device live
 A Plasma 6 widget that turns your Linux machine into a DLNA renderer
 able to receive audio pushed from a Synology NAS (Audio Station / DS audio),
 and lets you switch the output device live without interrupting playback.
 .
 Includes:
  * Plasma 6 applet (org.gmediarender.kde)
  * CLI helper (gmediarender-output) for querying/switching sinks
  * User systemd service for gmediarender
  * Configuration file